    "q-332749": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332749",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}(t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]){e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also constant, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
