    "q-333011": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333011",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t+2 \\\\ t+1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  | $\\,\\,{t}^{2}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $2$ |  |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |  |",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2({a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1})-({a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}) \\\\ {a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}-3){t}^{2}+(2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+4)t+(2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-4) \\\\ ({a}_{1}-1){t}^{2}+({b}_{1}-2)t+({c}_{1}+1)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}-3=0 \\\\ 2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+4=2{a}_{1} \\\\ 2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-4={b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1}-1=0 \\\\ {b}_{1}-2=2{a}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+1={b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the fourth equation and then substituting the corresponding values ​​into the first and fifth equations to solve for ${a}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=1,\\,{a}_{2}=-1,\\,{b}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe substitute these into the second equation to solve for ${b}_{2},$ and then into the sixth and third equations to solve for ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ We finally get\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=2,\\,{c}_{1}=-1,\\,{c}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+1 \\\\ -\\,{t}^{2}+2t-2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
