    "q-333597": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333597",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-0} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot {e}^{-0} \\\\ {e}^{-0}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2(0)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1 \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1=2 \\\\ {c}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=1.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
